# OSPF Multi-Area Configuration and Cost Manipulation Lab (NET 365)

## Overview

This lab demonstrates the configuration and analysis of **Open Shortest Path First (OSPF)** in a four-router Cisco network. The project focuses on establishing OSPF neighbor adjacencies, configuring multiple OSPF areas, advertising loopback and LAN networks, implementing passive interfaces, route summarization, and influencing path selection by modifying OSPF interface costs.

The lab concludes by verifying how OSPF recalculates shortest paths after interface costs are manually adjusted.

---

