## Passive Interfaces

Passive interfaces were configured on LAN and Loopback interfaces to prevent unnecessary OSPF Hello packets while still advertising connected networks.

| Router | Interface |
|---------|-----------|
| R1 | FastEthernet0/0 |
| R1 | Loopback0 |
| R2 | Loopback0 |
| R3 | Loopback0 |
| R4 | FastEthernet0/0 |
| R4 | Loopback0 |

---

## Route Summarization

R3, acting as the Area Border Router, summarizes Area 2 routes before advertising them into Area 0.

```cisco
area 2 range 200.10.82.0 255.255.255.224
```

Benefits:

- Smaller routing tables
- Reduced LSA flooding
- Improved scalability

